spes USB device mode (0183): sweet's DWC3 gadget (0072-0077) on SM6225, only with sweetusb=2.

On the spes platform sweet_usb.c now uses the SM6225 addresses (live FDT + gcc-khaje.c): GCC 0x1400000,
USB30_PRIM GDSC 0x1a004, CBCRs 0x1a010/0x1a014/0x1a018/0x1a084/0x1a080/0x1d008/0x9f000, DWC3 0x4e00000,
QSCRATCH 0x4ef8800. The SM7150 QUSB2 PHY is not read and the SM6225 SNPS femto PHY is not written: ABL's
overrides stay (run 1 on spesn: GDSC and clocks on, DWC3 3.30a halted). Before RUN_STOP the apps-SMMU
stream 0x120 is passed through with SpesModem's smmu_identity (as WLAN 0x1a0 / audio 0x1C1; ios-flame
found that ABL drops its stream match and the first DMA then resets the SoC); if that fails the
controller stays halted. smmu_identity is serialized (USB and the modem thread). On spes the driver
runs only with an explicit sweetusb=2, from the full UFS init and from the 0178 log-only diagnostic
init; it brings up ue0 192.168.7.2/24 (CDC-ECM) and the UDP live log to 192.168.7.1:5140.

